@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
<div>
    <p>
        Sure! Here's a simple and concise privacy policy for your movie website:

    </p>
    <p>
    <strong>Privacy Policy</strong>

        At [Your Movie Website Name], we value your privacy. This Privacy Policy outlines how we collect, use, and protect your personal information when you visit our website.

    <strong>Information Collection</strong>
        We collect basic information such as your IP address and browsing activity to improve your user experience and provide relevant content. We may use cookies to enhance site performance and analytics.

    <strong>Use of Information</strong>
        The information we collect helps us personalize your experience and improve our website’s functionality. We do not sell or share your personal data with third parties, except as required by law or to improve our services.

    <strong>Security</strong>
        We take reasonable measures to protect your personal information from unauthorized access, alteration, or destruction.

    <strong>Third-Party Links</strong>
        Our website may contain links to external sites. We are not responsible for the content or privacy practices of these sites.

    <strong>Your Rights</strong>
        You have the right to access, update, or request the deletion of your personal information at any time. For any questions, please contact us.

        By using our site, you agree to this Privacy Policy.

    </p>
    <p> Make sure to replace "[Your Movie Website Name]" with the actual name of your site!</p>
       
    

</div>
<p>Use this page to detail your site's privacy policy.</p>
